{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"DISK-CEILING DECISIONS (operator-approved 2026-09-02) + Defect-2 apply landed live.\n\n== Defect 2 (alarm/paging gap) — LIVE ==\nTerraform apply completed (acct 896586841071, us-east-1): both disk alarms now\ntreat_missing_data=breaching, verified live via describe-alarms. Plan was clean\n(0 add / 2 change / 0 destroy); root volume confirmed 60 GiB, no volume drift.\nChange 2523 (HCL) already MERGED. A host that stops publishing DiskUsed now PAGES\ninstead of self-clearing to OK — the gap that made the 5h outage blind is closed.\nCodification of root_volume_size_gb default 30->60 lands separately via Gerrit so\nthe daily drift check goes green (live=60 now matches).\n\n== Approved standing intent for Defect 1 (bounded ceiling) — FIRM ==\n1. Root volume stays at 60 GiB (temp recovery growth kept; +30 GiB gp3 = ~$2.40/mo,\n   below the operator negligible threshold).\n2. Option A APPROVED: per-accumulator HARD SIZE CAPS via native GC on each disk\n   consumer (docker overlay2/build cache, /var/tmp, journald, writable container\n   layers) — high-water-mark GC pattern (kubelet image GC, BuildKit --keep-storage/\n   maxUsedSpace, Nix min/max-free).\n   CONSTRAINT: each capped generator MUST have its OWN CloudWatch alarm so we have\n   per-generator capacity visibility (which generator is at its cap).\n3. Option C APPROVED as the long-term fix: code-review SCRATCH space (gate clones/\n   snapshots, e.g. /tmp/rebar-gate-snapshots) moves to a SEPARATE EBS volume so\n   review work can never fill the OS/root disk.\nOptions A and C + AC5 (/var/gerrit sibling scowlful-bovine-dragonfly) will be\ndecomposed into a design-reviewed infra epic (likely an ADR for the disk-ceiling\narchitecture), linked to this ticket. This ticket retains Defect 2 (alarm) which\nis now substantially complete pending induced-stop verification."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788373991754647001,"uuid":"354b76f1-36ad-4f8c-8a78-0edb09e09019"}